<title>USA: Nissan to offer 2,500 buyout packages - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Nissan to offer 2,500 buyout packages - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>All 2,500 of Nissan Motor Corp's North American sales, marketing and distribution employees will be offered early retirement and buyout packages, The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday, citing sources familiar with the situation.</p>
<p>A Nissan spokesman declined to comment on the Journal's story, which called the buyouts an unusual step to cut costs quickly.</p>
<p>It is unclear how many people Nissan hopes will accept the offers, the article said.</p>
<p>Sales of Nissan and Infinity brand cars and light trucks in the U.S. were down 3.4 percent in 1996, in contrast with robust sales of rival Toyota Motor Corp and Honda Motor Co vehicles, the story said.</p>
</text>
